{
  "about": "16 section and page grounds drawn in CSS (backgrounds.css). One class on a section, a wrapper, body or a visual's panel. The twelve section grounds set the page tokens for their children; the two page grounds (paper, topglow) set none and only paint. Each works on light and dark palettes and keeps ink 7:1 and muted 4.5:1 on its text zone (check.mjs measures it). pick.mjs deals a page's grounds (at most 2 beyond the flat tokens, no page ground; paper and grain are marked dealt:false and never dealt, since a ground with grain is the page's one effect; --effect also skips the grounds marked texture), for software, tech and gaming pages only (VI-41, VI-42): a product, service or place page is flat and no ground is listed for it (a product page with a technical subject asks with --kind tech and is dealt as software). Grounds list the sections they fit (sections): pick.mjs deals those; strict ones go nowhere else, byRole ones (band, field) also fit by role when the plan has none of their ids. Grounds marked coloured (band, field, stage; grain is never dealt) count toward the one coloured ground every page of five sections or more holds.",
  "version": 6,
  "weights": {
    "1": "calm: reads as the page",
    "2": "medium: a visible change of ground",
    "3": "loud: the one section a screen remembers"
  },
  "kinds": {
    "soft": "paints no colour of its own and fades into the page at the top and bottom; neighbours anything",
    "hard": "a band with its own colour and edges (add bg-inset for a rounded panel on the grid)",
    "page": "a ground for the whole page (body or one wrapper), not for one section",
    "panel": "a rounded panel behind one visual (bg-stage): vivid, with no text of its own; every word on it sits on a card"
  },
  "roles": [
    "hero",
    "body",
    "proof",
    "band",
    "close",
    "footer"
  ],
  "modifiers": {
    "bg-inset": "a hard ground as a rounded panel whose left and right edges sit on the container's",
    "bg-photo--left": "the photograph's scrim from the left, for words in the middle of the left side",
    "bg-photo--light": "the scrim from the light side and dark words, for a pale photograph",
    "bg-tint": "with bg-band or bg-field: the second tone is a pale tint of the accent's own colour (a mint for a teal accent) instead of the lit ground, so the band is coloured on a sand page",
    "bg-bleed": "on a dark page a band or a field is inset automatically (a pale slab is the brightest thing there); bg-bleed keeps it full-bleed"
  },
  "knobs": {
    "--g-hue": "the colour the tints lean to; default the accent with a hue guard (never violet or lavender)",
