<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap top-in">
    <div class="brand"><b>Effects library</b><span id="count"></span></div>
    <div class="controls">
      <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Palette kind">
        <button type="button" data-kind="light">Light</button>
        <button type="button" data-kind="dark">Dark</button>
        <button type="button" data-kind="colour">Colour</button>
      </div>
      <select class="select" id="pal" aria-label="Palette"></select>
      <button type="button" class="btn" id="pause" aria-pressed="false">Pause</button>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary" id="deal">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 4.5h2.2c1.2 0 2 .6 2.7 1.6l1.2 1.8c.7 1 1.5 1.6 2.7 1.6h2.2M11.6 2.5l2 2-2 2M2.5 11.5h2.2c.9 0 1.6-.3 2.2-.9M11.6 9.5l2 2-2 2M9.3 5.4c.6-.6 1.3-.9 2.1-.9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        Random pick
    </button>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero" id="hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Effects for hero frames and feature cards</h1>
        <p id="lede">Grain, dither, mesh, light, liquid, pattern and material grounds, drawn in code. Every colour comes from the page palette, and each page is dealt its own at random.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-tag"><span class="tag" id="hero-tag"><span>Hero</span> <b></b></span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="all">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <h2>All effects</h2>
          <p>Each one live, in the palette above. A tile names the effect, its family and the slots it is made for.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="filters" id="filters" role="group" aria-label="Family"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid" id="grid"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cards">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <div>
          <h2>On feature cards</h2>
          <p>Four effects dealt for card slots, each under a fragment from the UI kit. Random pick deals a new set.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Ask in plain words</h3>
          <p>Ask about any project or document. Every answer links to its source.</p>
          <div class="panel" data-card="0"><div class="slot" data-ui-load="chat"></div></div>
          <p class="ground">Ground: <b></b></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Hand off busy work</h3>
          <p>Show it a task once. It repeats the steps for you and asks before it publishes.</p>
          <div class="panel" data-card="1"><div class="slot" data-ui-load="cursor"></div></div>
          <p class="ground">Ground: <b></b></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>See what changed</h3>
          <p>A short weekly report shows what went up, what went down and why.</p>
          <div class="panel" data-card="2"><div class="slot" data-ui-load="stat"></div></div>
          <p class="ground">Ground: <b></b></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Connect your tools</h3>
          <p>Slack, Notion, Figma and GitHub connect in a few clicks.</p>
          <div class="panel" data-card="3"><div class="slot" data-ui-load="integrations"></div></div>
          <p class="ground">Ground: <b></b></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="foot">
    <div class="wrap foot-in"><div>
      <p>Every effect is drawn in code: no images, no video. It pauses when it leaves the screen, holds one still frame under reduced motion and falls back to a CSS picture without WebGL.</p>
      <p><a id="lab" href="lab.html">Parameters and layouts</a></p>
    </div></div>
  </footer>
</main>
