<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Moments</title>
<style>body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#111;background:#fff;padding:48px 24px}h1{font-size:28px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 8px}p.lead{color:#555;margin:0 0 32px;max-width:60ch}ul{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:grid;gap:12px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(320px,1fr))}li a{display:block;padding:16px 20px;border:1px solid #e5e5e5;border-radius:12px;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}li a:hover{border-color:#999}li b{font-weight:500}li span{display:block;color:#666;font-size:13px;margin:2px 0 6px}li p{margin:0;color:#333;font-size:14px}li p.ph{margin-top:6px;color:#666;font-size:13px}</style></head>
<body><h1>Moments</h1><p class="lead">13 creative moments, one or two a page on every kind; a place, product or service page is dealt only the photo- and type-led ones that list it (references/moments.md). Each link is a full demo page; the moment is marked data-moment in its source.</p><ul><li><a href="counter-rolls/demo.html"><b>Counter rolls</b> <span>text · statement · enter · tech, gaming, software</span><p>The digits of two to four proof figures roll once like an odometer when the row comes on screen, the right-most digit turning most; the strips rest on the real figures before and after, so the row never reads as zeros.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The figures stand.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="cursor-spotlight/demo.html"><b>Cursor spotlight</b> <span>hover · hero · pointer · tech, gaming, software</span><p>A soft light on the hero's ground follows the pointer with a short lag and shows a fine dot grid around it; it drifts back to its resting spot when the pointer leaves.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The light rests at its spot; there is no pointer.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="giant-type-pass/demo.html"><b>Giant type, picture passing</b> <span>scroll · statement · scroll · tech, gaming, software</span><p>Two to four words set at 12vw with a photograph showing through the letters under a 35% ink tint; the photograph passes upward through the type as the section crosses the screen.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The photograph stands still in the letters, the type smaller (19vw).</p></a></li>
<li><a href="iris-opens/demo.html"><b>Iris opens</b> <span>transition · section · scroll · tech, gaming, software</span><p>A section that sits on a new ground keeps that ground edge to edge; inside it an inset panel in the old ground (even gutter, card corners, never touching the section's edges) opens a disc in the middle of what is visible, widening with a hairline accent ring at its edge. Each heading, paragraph, button and picture stays hidden until the disc holds all of it, then fades in whole, so no word is ever cut.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The section stands on its own ground, no panel, no ring.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="letters-assemble/demo.html"><b>Letters assemble</b> <span>scroll · statement · scroll · tech, gaming, software</span><p>A statement of two to five words, set very large: its letters start scattered, shifted and turned, and fly into the line one after the other as the statement rises through the screen, whole before it reaches the middle.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The statement stands as written, in a smaller size.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="line-carries-colour/demo.html"><b>Line carries the colour</b> <span>transition · section · scroll · tech, gaming, software</span><p>A section that sits on a new ground keeps that ground edge to edge; inside it an inset panel in the old ground (even gutter, card corners, never touching the section's edges) is cleared by a one-pixel accent line that climbs through it from its foot to its top: below the line the section's own ground and words, above it the old ground. Each heading, paragraph, button and picture stays hidden until the line has passed above all of it, then fades in whole, so no word is ever cut.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The section stands on its own ground, no panel, no line.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="liquid-hover/demo.html"><b>Liquid hover</b> <span>liquid · hero, section · hover · WebGL · tech, gaming, software</span><p>The pointer pushes a photograph like the surface of water: the picture bends along the pointer's path with a wet shine and a hair of colour split, and the ripple diffuses away in a second or two, back to the plain picture.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The plain photograph, no canvas, no WebGL context.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="liquid-type/demo.html"><b>Liquid type</b> <span>liquid · hero, statement · pointer · tech, gaming, software</span><p>A very large headline ripples and stretches like type seen through water wherever the pointer crosses it, and settles back to crisp type within about a second; one SVG filter, only while it moves.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The headline stands as written; there is no pointer.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="marquee-row/demo.html"><b>Marquee row</b> <span>scroll · section · loop · tech, gaming, software</span><p>One row of client words, trades, cities or formats moves slowly sideways in a loop, fading at both edges; it pauses under the pointer and has a pause button.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The words stand in a wrapped row; nothing runs.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="photo-chapters/demo.html"><b>Photo chapters</b> <span>scroll · section · scroll · place, product, service</span><p>A short story in three to five photographs, one large frame at a time: the section holds on screen while, under its h2, one photograph the width of the page is uncovered by the next from its foot upward, settling from a slight zoom, and a panel in the page's ground on the photograph's lower left changes to that chapter (its number, a title and two lines). Each chapter has about two thirds of a screen of scroll: the wipe takes under half of it and the photograph holds for the rest. Live at every width on a screen 600px or taller, phones included.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: It runs on a phone held upright (one photograph at a time, the panel across its foot); a phone turned sideways, under 600px tall, gets the chapters stacked, each photograph over its words.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="picture-develops/demo.html"><b>Picture develops</b> <span>transition · section, hero · enter · place, product, service</span><p>One large photograph develops once as it comes on screen. On a place, product or service page (look "film") it comes up out of the paper like a print in the developer tray: a faint grey print at first, its darks arriving before its light tones, then its colour, while it settles from a slight zoom, about 1.6 s. The halftone look ("print", a two-tone dot print in the page's ground and ink giving way to the photograph) is not dealt: tech leaves this moment out, so it is kept only as opts look "print".</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: The film look runs on a phone too (one picture, a filter and a transform, once); the print look shows the photograph.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="pinned-chapters/demo.html"><b>Pinned chapters</b> <span>scroll · section · scroll · tech, gaming, software, product, service</span><p>A feature section holds on screen for two screens of scroll while its three steps open one at a time at the left and one frame at the right changes to each step's picture with a short crossfade.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: Nothing is pinned: each step stands with its title, two lines and its visual under it.</p></a></li>
<li><a href="word-highlight/demo.html"><b>Statement lights up</b> <span>scroll · statement · scroll · tech, gaming, software, place, product, service</span><p>One large statement rests at half ink (readable, about 4 to 1) and turns to ink word by word as it crosses the middle of the screen, a strong word to the accent; it runs back on the way up.</p><p class="ph">Phone and reduced motion: It runs on a phone as on a desktop (one paragraph's colours); under reduced motion the whole statement is in ink, the accent word in the accent.</p></a></li></ul></body></html>
</file>

